# Every variable below is required. The set and its resolution order are defined
# once, in `src/reporting_agent/config.py` as `REQUIRED_ENV_VARS`; `Config.from_env()`
# reads them at process start and raises `MissingConfigError` naming the first one
# that is absent, empty or whitespace-only.
#
# Placeholders only — copy to `.env` (git-ignored) and fill in. No real credential
# value belongs in this file.
#
# Deliberately absent: the Azure `tenant_id`, `client_id` and `client_secret`, and the
# per-invocation `run_id`, `actor_id`, `progress_url` and `progress_token`. Those
# arrive in the invoke payload's `context` — an environment variable is the wrong
# lifetime for a per-customer credential, and a run must never authenticate as the
# container's own identity.
# Region for the S3 artifact writes and every other AWS client.
# Example: us-east-1
AWS_REGION=<aws-region>
# Private S3 bucket holding snapshots, the raw archive, figure ledgers, verification
# results and the rendered .docx / .pdf, under an `actor_id` prefix.
RPT_ARTIFACT_BUCKET=<artifact-bucket-name>
# Bedrock model that writes narrative prose, and only prose — it never produces a
# number that reaches a document. Agent-side only: this must not appear in
# `app/.env.example`, where a guard asserts the key set equals the app's own required
# set. Production runs Kimi K3, which Bedrock offers only through an inference
# profile, so the id carries the profile's prefix. Example: us.moonshotai.kimi-k3
RPT_PROSE_MODEL_ID=<bedrock-model-id>
# OPTIONAL — leave unset unless the app's certificate is issued by a private authority.
# A PEM file of additional trusted roots, mounted into the container. `httpx` verifies
# the progress callback against certifi with an explicit `cafile`, so SSL_CERT_FILE and
# REQUESTS_CA_BUNDLE do not reach it and this is the only way to add a root. Unset means
# the default trust store, which is what a publicly trusted certificate needs.
# Example: /etc/ssl/private-ca/root.pem
RPT_CA_BUNDLE=<pem-file-path-or-unset>
# OPTIONAL — the Bedrock model the `chat` command answers with. Unset means the prose
# model above. Example: us.moonshotai.kimi-k3
RPT_CHAT_MODEL_ID=<bedrock-model-id-or-unset>
# OPTIONAL — the Bedrock guardrail the `chat` command runs every question through (prompt
# attack filter). Chat refuses to start while either is unset: an
# unguarded chat fails closed rather than answering. Example: gr-abc123def456 / 1
RPT_CHAT_GUARDRAIL_ID=<guardrail-id-or-unset>
RPT_CHAT_GUARDRAIL_VERSION=<guardrail-version-or-unset>
# OPTIONAL — a fast model with no reasoning phase that writes the one sentence Ask shows
# while the answer model is still thinking ("I'll compare CPU use across…"). It runs
# behind the same guardrail and may not write a digit. Unset: no such sentence.
# Production: us.moonshotai.kimi-k3
RPT_INTENT_MODEL_ID=<bedrock-model-id-or-unset>
